The emulator, platform and region definitions in this directory are taken from
Playnite and are used under the MIT licence reproduced below. They are data
files, unmodified: GameBox compiles them into emulators.json at build time and
reads them at scan and launch time.

  Upstream: https://github.com/JosefNemec/Playnite
  Path:     source/Playnite/Emulation
  Files:    Emulators/*/emulator.yaml, Platforms.yaml, Regions.yaml

Each emulator.yaml describes one emulator: its profiles, the platforms each
profile covers, the ROM extensions it accepts, a regular expression matching its
executable, and the command line to start a game with. That last part is what
GameBox could not do on its own - it launched every emulator with a bare image
path and no arguments.

